    "statementMarkdown": "For $n \\geq 2$, an equilateral triangle is divided into $n^{2}$ congruent smaller equilateral triangles. Determine all ways in which real numbers can be assigned to the $\\frac{(n+1)(n+2)}{2}$ vertices so that three such numbers sum to zero whenever the three vertices form a triangle with edges parallel to the sides of the big triangle.\n",
